      "artist": "McKay Savage from London, UK",
      "description": "Kapitan Keling Mosque in Georgetown is a beautiful historic mosque of the Tamil Muslim community, founded in 1801 and expanded with its Mughul-style architecture in circa 1910.\n\nWhat was remarkable about Georgetown was that in 10 blocks and 1 square km we passed religious centres for both Chinese Buddhist, Taoist and Confucian temples, both Tamil and Malay Muslim Mosques, Tamil Hindu temples, and both Protestant and Catholic Christian Churches. Nowhere have I seen so many religions going about their days side-by-side in so tightly packed a space.",
